Z||000003||JBGehling||11-27-2000||07:37 PM||||Hey Vietnow, I can't help you with the Fiero factory and such, but I can help you with some of the later questions...<BR>C=coupe (4 cylinder)<BR>GT= Gran Touring<P>HP<BR>     84       85        86      87       88<P>C= 92@4000  92@4000  92@4000  96@4800 98@4800<P>GT= --   140@5200 140@5200  135@4500 135@4500<P>Torque<BR>    84      85         86       87      88<P>C134@2800 134@2800 134@2800 135@3200 135@3200<P>GT --   170@3600  170@3600  165@3600 165@3600<P>I think everyone agrees that the best year for Fieros was 1988, of course, this year is also a good deal more $ than the other years as well.<BR>Not sure what year is the most upgradeable.<BR>I'm sure after-market turbos are offered somewhere... anyone?<P>Josh<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||JBGehling||11-27-2000||07:43 PM||||BTW, no GT's were offered in 84...||||reg||1
